-- Consequences of tree packing: a 2k-edge-connected graph has k disjoint
-- spanning trees, and a 3-edge-connected graph has three spanning trees with
-- no edge common to all three, found in the graph with every edge doubled.
-- Part of Cumulus, the Grace17 mathematics library.
